{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-tm-heavy-atom-examples-table2-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:tm-heavy-atom-examples-table2-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 2 from tm-heavy-atom-examples","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tm-heavy-atom-examples"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"tm-heavy-atom-examples-table2-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"tbl:tm-heavy-atom-examples-table2-data\"></a>\n<strong>Table.</strong> <em>Data table 2 from tm-heavy-atom-examples</em></p>\n<p>Magic-number lookup for the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^{14}\\mathrm{C} \\to {}^{14}\\mathrm{N}</code>\ndecay: the parent's neutron count <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N = 8</code> is a magic number\n(<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_{\\mathrm{out}} = 0</code>), so its outermost neutron shell is closed and\nthe <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta^-</code> transition breaks that closure.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"center\">Nucleon count</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_{\\leq}</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_{\\mathrm{out}}</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Shell size</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z = 6</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">8 - 2 = 6</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N = 8</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">8</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^{\\dagger}</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">8 - 2 = 6</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z' = 7</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N' = 7</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">5</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">6</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_{\\leq}</code> is the largest magic number not exceeding the count,\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_{\\mathrm{out}}</code> is the outer-shell occupancy (the count minus\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m_{\\leq}</code>, which vanishes when the count is magic), and Shell size is\nthe capacity of the shell containing the count.\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^{\\dagger}</code> Closed shell: the neutron count is magic, so the\noutermost shell is filled.</p>\n"}
